            "notes": "Lots of yap this round's notes sorry anyone reading these LOL\n\n[Home Remedy](item_de68ba66-26d5-4136-a0c1-6396d3f1b0c7) is such an underrated power, IMO. Making any ally (including yourself!) affected by nade get not only the usual boosted healing, but additional overhealth on top of that is *not* to be underestimated.\nThis either can give you enough time to heal your critical tank currently frontlining back to full HP while being focused, or can help YOU win 1v1s way more than you'd think. Fighting someone but you're low or about to take a bunch of burst? Nade the floor next to both of you and now you can be healed easier, have a bunch of extra HP, and whoever you're fighting no longer can get any healing. It's a very powerful tool.\n\nIf I can, I like getting [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) (see section below) pretty early on, but some games I find focusing a bit of WP and survivability this round is better, and others I try to get [Cluster Core](item_c63cd7ba-b71c-4503-bdb6-4ef0b0a4bdbb) ASAP instead. It all sorta depends on the game - if your team groups up a lot or brawls with the enemies close together, then [Cluster Core](item_c63cd7ba-b71c-4503-bdb6-4ef0b0a4bdbb) could be the way to go. If *you're* getting dove more often, then [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) gives you better long-term survivability. Heck, if you find that you can't keep your tank alive sometimes in fights because you run out of ammo as they take consistent damage, then getting [Unscoped Resources](item_64c401f6-7508-4fc7-ac3a-93c9f3f57e2b) early on might be better for you. \n\nAlso, to be clearer on the blue survival items; I'll more often go for [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016), but if you have a tank with a lot of armor and thus the enemies might grab/the opponents are in general more likely to take [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27), I'll lean more towards [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0)\n\n[Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) is an item listed under Ability, but really, it's a confused Survival item if you ask me. Even if you don't care for AP, (and it only does so much for our build here), giving you 50 extra *armor* and the ability to regen 25 armor/s every time you use an ability is absolutely amazing. \nThis is one reason why we never, ever sell [Dash Boots](item_1ec670c7-a465-4ca0-9d16-aeeedab7894e). Normally, Ana's really long cooldowns would make [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) not that great of an item, but with another ability on a 3s cooldown, this goes from \"eh\" to \"great\", and puts your survivability way up.",
