            "notes": "Personally, I'd prioritize getting [Cluster Core](item_c63cd7ba-b71c-4503-bdb6-4ef0b0a4bdbb) in most games, because it really helps to reduce your nade cooldown, and your nade can be a fight-winning ability - or at least make it so the enemy feels like your team never dies. However, you will probably have to sack at least a little WP, especially if you don't have 30k, OR some survivability, though you can exchange [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) for both [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0) and [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016) if you really need to - it won't quite provide the same benefits, but it's close.\n\nAll* of the optional items are good items to take, though it may not be super likely you're able to fit them into your build. \n*The ONE exception is [Target Tracker](item_450e11f9-34b6-40c6-b810-0a9ad6c7a093), which I only take if I also have [Cluster Core](item_c63cd7ba-b71c-4503-bdb6-4ef0b0a4bdbb), as I mostly just choose that item for the extended nade duration.\n\nOccasionally, I might take [Unscoped Resources](item_64c401f6-7508-4fc7-ac3a-93c9f3f57e2b) this round instead of [Cluster Core](item_c63cd7ba-b71c-4503-bdb6-4ef0b0a4bdbb), but it's uncommon as I find CC more generally helpful and UR costs more.",
