            "notes": "To be clear on how [Sleep Regimen](item_28934e4f-0668-482e-b10d-a5d557cc3b1e)'s mechanics work:\n1. You keep this health throughout every round, it just keeps stacking up\n2. It counts *every sleep you've gotten in the game so far*, so if you've slept 10 total enemies in the first four rounds, you'll get 150 extra health immediately. \nBecause of this, this is a great power, and what really helps you reach 600+ HP in the late rounds. \nBut, if you truly have not hit basically any sleeps so far, and don't think you will be, then [My Turn](item_5cea2ccb-c889-4447-8a84-c704c1da1521) is also a good power to add to your survivability and lethality, especially since s17 it lasts the entire duration of nano.\n\nBoth [Unscoped Resources](item_64c401f6-7508-4fc7-ac3a-93c9f3f57e2b) and [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8) are great items to take, (NC over other survival items as it synergizes well with [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) while also giving you a bit of WP), but they also both cost 11k, so instead this round I've added some blue items, but if you have enough and would rather just take one of the purple items instead then go for it.\nI'd lean more towards [Unscoped Resources](item_64c401f6-7508-4fc7-ac3a-93c9f3f57e2b) first, as you'll likely to have gotten a big chunk of extra health through [Sleep Regimen](item_28934e4f-0668-482e-b10d-a5d557cc3b1e) this round, but neither option is bad.",
