            "created_at": "2025-07-27T04:15:51.099217+00:00",
            "notes": "[My Turn](item_5cea2ccb-c889-4447-8a84-c704c1da1521) is just a good power choice, giving you more survivability and ability to kill in a situation that you might have otherwise run out of cooldowns, and though it's usually my go-to, the other options aren't bad either:\n- [Our Turn](item_6e0fdb41-c00f-41d9-8ec2-1246b34a539a): Nano for your whole team (within range + LOS) with 75% of the normal duration is great (obviously, this does not apply to yourself)\n- [Your Full Potential](item_f03b3a26-0d1b-46bc-85e6-92f060b53b4e): Got a Zarya 70% of the way to grav? Nano them and they'll have it immediately! A crit health soldier close to visor? Use your ult and they'll have it and overhealth to spare!\n- [Time Out](item_34fc2f6c-ecd9-489e-98ca-d08f3eb2fac1): 50% slow is probably even slower than you think it is. It's *incredibly* slow. I will say in my limited testing of this power, sometimes the self-knockback is a little annoying over helpful, but this is a good power to take if your nades have been hitting enemies. \n\nThe final build! Same things apply this round as did last, I'd recommend swapping out [Unscoped Resources](item_64c401f6-7508-4fc7-ac3a-93c9f3f57e2b) if you wanted one of the optional items. \nYou could also possibly, with how high your HP is now, swap out [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) for [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98), as 3% of your life is more worth it at 600+ hp, but I generally don't.",
